Add missing DeprecationMessage::setFile() setter.

LibraryDeprecationAnalyzer calls $is_deprecated->setFile() whenever
isLibraryDeprecated() returns a DeprecationMessage (a library reference
without an extension name, or an exception from LibraryDiscoveryParser),
but upgrade_status 4.3.10 no longer has the setter (4.3.8 did). This makes
`drush upgrade_status:analyze` fatal with "Call to undefined method
Drupal\upgrade_status\DeprecationMessage::setFile()".
$is_deprecated->setFile($name) on a DeprecationMessage instance, but the
class only exposes a getter. This makes `drush upgrade_status:analyze`
fatal with "Call to undefined method
Drupal\upgrade_status\DeprecationMessage::setFile()" for any extension
whose Twig templates attach a deprecated library.

--- a/src/DeprecationMessage.php
+++ b/src/DeprecationMessage.php
@@ -76,6 +76,19 @@
   public function getFile(): string {
     return $this->file;
   }

+  /**
+   * Sets the file related to the deprecation message.
+   *
+   * @param string $file
+   *   The file related to the deprecation message.
+   *
+   * @return $this
+   */
+  public function setFile(string $file): static {
+    $this->file = $file;
+    return $this;
+  }
+
